{"id":"f117e6fe-2c93-4916-809a-246f483afc34","object":"chat.completion","created":1785027069,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be dict\\\")\\n    if 'tokens' not in case or not isinstance(case['tokens'], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"tokens missing or not list\\\")\\n    if 'calls' not in case or not isinstance(case['calls'], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls missing or not list\\\")\\n    tokens = case['tokens']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    for c in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call not dict\\\")\\n        for key in ('call_id', 'start', 'end', 'score', 'replacement_tokens'):\\n            if key not in c:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call missing '{key}'\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(c['call_id'], str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id not string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(c['start'], int) or not isinstance(c['end'], int):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"start/end not int\\\")\\n        if c['start'] < 0 or c['end'] > len(tokens) or c['start'] >= c['end']:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"invalid span\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(c['score'], (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"score not number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(c['replacement_tokens'], list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in c['replacement_tokens']):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"replacement_tokens invalid\\\")\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda x: (-x['score'], x['start'], x['call_id']))\\n    selected = []\\n    selected_intervals = []\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        start, end = c['start'], c['end']\\n        overlap = False\\n        for (s, e) in selected_intervals:\\n            if not (end <= s or start >= e):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(c)\\n            selected_intervals.append((start, end))\\n    selected_sorted = sorted(selected, key=lambda x: (x['start'], x['call_id']))\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected_sorted]\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)\\n    for c in sorted(selected, key=lambda x: -x['start']):\\n        start, end, repl = c['start'], c['end'], c['replacement_tokens']\\n        result_tokens = result_tokens[:start] + repl + result_tokens[end:]\\n    return {\\\"selected_call_ids\\\": selected_call_ids, \\\"tokens\\\": result_tokens}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that follows the specification. The task: AGENT-TF-02. From the payload, we have tokens (list of strings) and calls (list of objects with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). The output must be a dict with selected_call_ids (list of strings) and tokens (list of strings) after applying replacements from accepted calls, interleaving.\n\nThe algorithm: \n1. Filter calls: rank by descending score, then ascending start, then call_id string? The description: \"Rank candidates by descending score, start position, then call ID.\" So sort: (-score, start, call_id).\n2. Greedily accept calls that do not overlap with already selected spans. Overlap: intervals [start, end) presumably? start inclusive, end exclusive? Need to check typical token indices. The calls have start and end. In the example, start=1, end=3 covers tokens[1], tokens[2]? Likely start inclusive, end exclusive. Overlap if intervals intersect.\n3. Apply replacements from right to left (i.e., descending start) to avoid offset shifts.\n4. Return selected_call_ids (sorted by start? \"Order accepted calls by source start for reporting.\" So selected_call_ids list in order of ascending start (and then maybe by call_id for ties? But start likely unique per call? Not necessarily. We'll sort selected calls by start, then call_id).\n5. Tokens: start with original tokens list. For each accepted call in descending start order (i.e., reverse order of start), replace the substring tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens list. Concatenate: tokens[:start] + replacement_tokens + tokens[end:].\n\nImplementation details:\n- Input case is a dict with keys: tokens, calls. Also _case_nonce present in fixtures but not required.\n- Validate fields: tokens must be list, calls list of dicts with required fields: call_id (string), start (int), end (int), score (float), replacement_tokens (list of strings). Raise ValueError if missing or invalid.\n- Return dict with selected_call_ids and tokens.\n\nEdge cases: overlapping calls, empty calls, no accepted calls.\n\nWe'll write solve(case) in Python.\n\nNow produce JSON with single key \"implementation\" containing the source code as a JSON string.\n\nLet's write code.\n\nEnsure we escape properly for JSON: newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, quotes as \\\".\n\nWrite function:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # validate case\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be dict\")\n    if 'tokens' not in case or not isinstance(case['tokens'], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"tokens missing or not list\")\n    if 'calls' not in case or not isinstance(case['calls'], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls missing or not list\")\n    tokens = case['tokens']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    # validate each call\n    for c in calls:\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"call not dict\")\n        for key in ('call_id', 'start', 'end', 'score', 'replacement_tokens'):\n            if key not in c:\n                raise ValueError(f\"call missing '{key}'\")\n        if not isinstance(c['call_id'], str):\n            raise ValueError(\"call_id not string\")\n        if not isinstance(c['start'], int) or not isinstance(c['end'], int):\n            raise ValueError(\"start/end not int\")\n        if c['start'] < 0 or c['end'] > len(tokens) or c['start'] >= c['end']:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid span\")\n        if not isinstance(c['score'], (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"score not number\")\n        if not isinstance(c['replacement_tokens'], list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in c['replacement_tokens']):\n            raise ValueError(\"replacement_tokens invalid\")\n    \n    # sort calls by (descending score, ascending start, call_id)\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda x: (-x['score'], x['start'], x['call_id']))\n    \n    selected = []\n    # intervals: set of (start, end)\n    selected_intervals = []  # list of (start, end)\n    for c in sorted_calls:\n        start, end = c['start'], c['end']\n        # check overlap with any selected\n        overlap = False\n        for (s, e) in selected_intervals:\n            if not (end <= s or start >= e):  # intervals overlap\n                overlap = True\n                break\n        if not overlap:\n            selected.append(c)\n            selected_intervals.append((start, end))\n    \n    # order selected by source start (ascending), then call_id\n    selected_sorted = sorted(selected, key=lambda x: (x['start'], x['call_id']))\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected_sorted]\n    \n    # apply replacements right to left (descending start)\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)  # copy\n    # sort selected by start descending\n    for c in sorted(selected, key=lambda x: -x['start']):\n        start, end, repl = c['start'], c['end'], c['replacement_tokens']\n        # replace slice\n        result_tokens = result_tokens[:start] + repl + result_tokens[end:]\n    \n    return {\"selected_call_ids\": selected_call_ids, \"tokens\": result_tokens}\n\nMake sure to import nothing outside standard lib.\n\nNow produce JSON response.\n\nFinal check: The output schema requires \"selected_call_ids\" and \"tokens\". Both are present. types match.\n\nWrite the source as a string, escape.\n\nWe'll output:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\\n\"}\n\nLet's produce."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1654,"completion_tokens":1911,"total_tokens":3565,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1263},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":118},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}